# NOTICE

superred-claim-mcp-tool-injection

This module red-teams the MCP (Model Context Protocol) tool supply chain as a
superred SecurityClaim. All code and the bundled poison payloads are original to
this module and licensed MIT (see LICENSE). No third-party dataset or source is
vendored.

## Poison payloads

The illustrative tool-poisoning payloads in `src/mcp_tool_injection_claim/poisons.py`
(5) are original content authored for this module — canonical tool-poisoning
patterns (hidden instructions in a tool's advertised description), not copied from
any dataset. They exist so the claim is runnable and testable out of the box and to
seed an optimizer; they are not a benchmark. Supply your own via
`mcp_tool_injection_claim(poisons=...)`.

## Protocol under test (not vendored)

- Model Context Protocol (MCP) and its Python SDK — https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk
  (MIT, © Anthropic, PBC). This module and the paired `superred-target-mcp-agent`
  depend on the SDK; no SDK code is vendored.

## Citation

When reporting results, describe the MCP server, tools, and agent model used —
tool-injection susceptibility depends on all three and is point-in-time (hosted
models change).
